      "id": 2,
      "claim": "An elevator system consists of a vertical shaft that supports the car and a mechanism that transports supplies between floors.",
      "evidence": "Engineering descriptions of elevators note that the shaft provides the structural framework while the elevator car moves goods or people vertically between levels.",
      "weight": 0.35,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Because the elevator combines both a supporting structure (the shaft) and vertical transport of materials, it parallels the dual role of a plant stem more closely than the other options.",
      "evidence": "Analogy reasoning: stem ↔ shaft (support) and stem ↔ elevator car (transport) versus alternatives that lack one of these functions.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1, 2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Option A (anchor) provides only static support and no transport function, so it matches only part of the stem’s role.",
      "evidence": "An anchor holds a boat in place but does not convey materials between parts, unlike a stem.",
      "weight": 0.025,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
